MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 118414957}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ee0300430bca0e244bd52e1231433524, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AutopilotAgentLesson
  title: Autopilot agent
  instructions: 'The drone flies the mission by itself: take-off, the gate loop at
    6 m, return and land. Watch from any camera (C). Move the sticks to take over;
    Backspace restarts the agent.'
  discipline: Agent
  goal: Watch the drone fly the whole mission by itself, then take over whenever
    you like.
  steps:
  - Start the drill - the drone arms and takes off on its own.
  - Press C to watch from the chase, pilot and FPV cameras.
  - Move a stick at any time to take control.
  - Press Backspace to hand the mission back to the agent.
  skill: What a smooth, correct flight looks like - copy the heights, speeds and
    turns you see.
  tip: Do not just watch the drone move. Watch where it slows down and how wide it
    turns, then fly the same line yourself.
  controls: C = change camera,   move any stick = take over,   Backspace = restart
    the agent
